# PART 1 — Review of [VACUITY_CONVENTION.md](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/VACUITY_CONVENTION.md)

## Mechanism Comparison: Script-Parsed Doc Tags vs. Lean Attributes vs. Doc Tags Read in Lean Meta Code (`findDocString?`)

Before scoring Sections 1–5, we must decide the mechanism by the best long-term design under [trust_ban.sh](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh):

| Mechanism | How it works | Why it succeeds or fails long-term |
|---|---|---|
| **(A) Script-parsed doc tags** (regex over source, like the surface pass of [rules.py](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/scripts/spec/rules.py)) | Python scans `/-- ... -/` comments above `theorem` and `example`. | **Shortcut — reject as sole mechanism.** Cannot inspect elaborated `Expr`s (`ConstantInfo.type`, `ConstantInfo.value!`), cannot verify that an `Instance` actually applies the law or instantiates all hypotheses with closed terms, cannot verify that a `Planted` example refutes the conclusion rather than a premise, and is not rename-safe without an environment lookup. |
| **(B) Custom Lean attributes** (`@[law]`, `@[instance_of ``law]`, `@[planted ``law]`) inside `ConcreteSpec` | Parametric attributes registered via `registerBuiltinAttribute` or `registerParametricAttribute`. | **Conflicts with `ConcreteSpec` kernel purity ([trust_ban.sh](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh#L15-L34)).** Defining custom attributes inside `ConcreteSpec` requires `import Lean` and `initialize`, both banned by [trust_ban.sh](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh#L17-L29) so `ConcreteSpec` stays `Init`-only for `lean4export` and external kernel checkers. Furthermore, standard Lean `example` declarations discard their constant after elaboration unless rewritten or hooked. |
| **(C) Doc-comment tags in `ConcreteSpec` + `lean_lex.py examples` rewrite + Lean 4.34.1 meta-code gate (`findDocString?` + `ConstantInfo` inspection)** | Tags live in `/-- ... -/` directly on the `theorem`, `structure`/`class`, or `example` in `ConcreteSpec` (one home, no side list). The gate uses [lean_lex.py](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/scripts/proofs/lean_lex.py#L229-L263) (`examples` mode, already used by [rules.sh](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/scripts/spec/rules.sh#L33-L45)) to turn each `example` into `noncomputable def «⟪example⟫FILE:LINE»` (which preserves the preceding `/-- ... -/` docstring), elaborates once, and runs a Lean meta module (`import Lean`) *outside* `ConcreteSpec` that reads `findDocString? env declName`, resolves every backticked `` `Name `` in `env` (`env.find?`), and inspects `ci.type` and `ci.value!`. | **Best long-term design.** Zero `import Lean` or `initialize` in `ConcreteSpec`; single source of truth in doc comments right on the declarations; 100% rename-safe (unresolved `` `Name `` fails the gate, and we additionally require the `Instance` proof term to contain `.const lawName _`); full kernel `Expr` inspection of both theorems and examples. |

