## The Gate's Own Planted Negative Controls (`scripts/proofs/vacuity_controls.sh`)

Following the pattern in [`scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/scripts/proofs/trust_ban.sh#L156-L185) and [`scripts/spec/rules.sh`](file:///home/unbalancedparen/projects/gates-briefs/n2/scripts/spec/rules.sh#L69-L163), `vacuity.sh --self-test` (or a dedicated probe module elaborated in the temp workspace) runs **9 planted negative controls** in a single batch elaboration and asserts that `vacuity.lean` fails each one by naming the exact offending declaration and error code:

| # | Planted Control | Concrete Lean Probe | Required Gate Failure Output |
|---|---|---|---|
| **C1** | `Law` with no `Instance:` | `/-- Law. -/ theorem ctl_no_instance (n : Nat) (h : n > 0) : n + 1 > 1 := by omega` (with only a `Planted:` example) | `FAIL [NO_INSTANCE] ConcreteSpec.Control.ctl_no_instance` |
| **C2** | `Law` with no `Planted:` | `/-- Law. -/ theorem ctl_no_planted (n : Nat) (h : n > 0) : n + 1 > 1 := by omega` (with only an `Instance:` example) | `FAIL [NO_PLANTED] ConcreteSpec.Control.ctl_no_planted` |
| **C3** | `Planted:` whose statement is not a negation | `/-- Planted: `ctl_pos_planted`. -/ example : 1 + 1 = 2 := rfl` | `FAIL [PLANTED_NOT_NEGATION] ConcreteSpec.Control.ctl_pos_planted (at FILE:LINE)` |
| **C4** | Tag naming a nonexistent law | `/-- Instance: `ConcreteSpec.NoSuchLaw`. -/ example : True := trivial` | `FAIL [UNKNOWN_LAW_REF] ConcreteSpec.NoSuchLaw (at FILE:LINE)` |
| **C5** | `Helper` that is public / unreferenced by any `Law` | `/-- Helper. -/ theorem ctl_dead_helper (n : Nat) : n + 0 = n := by omega` | `FAIL [HELPER_PUBLIC_OR_UNUSED] ConcreteSpec.Control.ctl_dead_helper` |
| **C6** | `Obligation` that is a `theorem` | `/-- Obligation. -/ theorem ctl_thm_obligation (t : Target) (h : t.WellFormed) : 0 < t.addrBits := h.1` | `FAIL [OBLIGATION_IS_THEOREM] ConcreteSpec.Control.ctl_thm_obligation` |
| **C7** | **Projection / by-definition `Law`** | `/-- Law. -/ theorem ctl_proj_law (t : Target) (h : t.WellFormed) : 0 < t.addrBits ∧ t.addrBits ≤ 8 * t.ptrSize := ⟨h.1, h.2.1⟩` (even with `Instance:` and `Planted:` attached!) | `FAIL [TRIVIAL_PROJECTION_OR_RFL] ConcreteSpec.Control.ctl_proj_law` |
| **C8** | **`Law` with an unsatisfiable hypothesis** (or degenerate empty-witness instance) | `/-- Law. -/ theorem ctl_unsat_hyp (n : Nat) (h1 : n < 5) (h2 : n > 10) : n = 42 := by omega` — any `Instance:` either cannot typecheck if required to apply `ctl_unsat_hyp`, or if someone writes an `Instance:` that doesn't apply `ctl_unsat_hyp` (or uses an empty list `[]` for `∀ x ∈ l, x < 5 ∧ x > 10`), the gate rejects it! | `FAIL [INSTANCE_DOES_NOT_APPLY_LAW / DEGENERATE_INSTANCE] ConcreteSpec.Control.ctl_unsat_hyp` |
| **C9** | **`Planted:` counter-example that only breaks the premise** | For `ctl_law (t : Target) (h : t.WellFormed) : ...`, `/-- Planted: `ctl_law`. -/ example : ¬ ({ linuxX8664 with ptrAlign := 6 }).WellFormed := by decide` (negates the hypothesis `t.WellFormed` instead of showing the conclusion fails) | `FAIL [PLANTED_REFUTES_PREMISE] ConcreteSpec.Control.ctl_law (at FILE:LINE)` |

Notice that because all 9 controls can be placed in one synthetic `ConcreteSpec/Control.lean` module in the temp copy and elaborated in a single `lake env lean` invocation, testing all 9 negative controls takes **~1.5 seconds total**, not $9 \times$ full builds!

